    "export_probe": {
      "item_id": "accumulated_deuterated_methane_prefill_count",
      "name": "accumulated_deuterated_methane_prefill_count",
      "unit": "1",
      "source_path": "summary/gas_injection_prefill/methane_deuterated/value",
      "source_description": "Value",
      "source_unit": "1",
      "documentation": "This quantity is the cumulative amount of deuterated methane introduced during the plasma prefill phase, expressed as an equivalent-electron inventory. It represents neutral CD4 molecules before plasma breakdown, not the post-breakdown gas-injection inventory.\n\nThe equivalent-electron count is defined by\n\n$$\nN_{e,\\rm eq}^{\\rm prefill} = \\int_{t_0}^{t_b} \\dot{N}_{e,\\rm eq}^{\\rm CD_4}(t)\\,dt = 10N_{\\rm CD_4}^{\\rm prefill}\n$$\n\nwhere $N_{e,\\rm eq}^{\\rm prefill}$ is the accumulated equivalent-electron inventory, $\\dot{N}_{e,\\rm eq}^{\\rm CD_4}$ is the [deuterated methane source rate](name:deuterated_methane_source_rate), $t_0$ and $t_b$ delimit prefill before breakdown, and $N_{\\rm CD_4}^{\\rm prefill}$ is the accumulated number of CD4 molecules. The factor ten is the total electron count of one fully ionizable CD4 molecule. The species-resolved quantity contributes to the [accumulated total prefill gas count](name:accumulated_total_prefill_gas_count), which sums equivalent-electron inventories across gas species."
    },
